  "id": "public-self-consciousness",
  "term": "public self-consciousness",
  "definition": "Public self-consciousness is an increased awareness of how one appears to other people, along with sensitivity to being evaluated by them. It involves concern about social approval, image, and possible damage to one’s reputation in settings where feedback from others is visible.",
